  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-11-19T18:32:38.845Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Basically a way to attach items or props to your avatar by making an empty object in the desired location of the equipment and desired rotation and giving it a component (let's call it VRC_EquipmentSlot for now) and the component allows you to specify the name of the slot the location is, this is written in and not chosen from a dropdown menu. Then you can upload it to an avatar and go on to make an equipment item. It requires an EquipmentDescriptor which allows you to choose which slots it can go in to (written in text) and you can choose from a dropdown which hand should be able to pick it up, options are: Both (default), Right, Left. So you could as an example have a sword and a shield equipment slot on your back and the you can only pick up the sword with the hand you specify. You should also be able to add triggers to equipment but they would be limited in that they can only execute things on themselves, Mostly used to toggle an animation, so if you have an equipment that is a watergun as an example you could use the trigger button while the equipment is held to trigger its animation. Im thinking that the triggers could be activated with single click or being held down, You should also be able to choose which object of the equipment is picked up, like if you have a gun you might want it to be in a holster while not picked up. When you are done with your equipment you can upload it to your equipment warderobe which is a new tab in the ingame menu, here you can see all the equipment slots on your avatar both visually and by text (if 2 are in the same place like a sword and shield) and when a slot has been chosen, all of youre equipment that work with that slot will be shown and everything else will be hidden, then you can simply choose a piece of equipment and add it to your character.",
